WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
MineBit is an NFT marketplace
for Minecraft builds.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.360
Minecraft is all about creativity.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.720
Players make huge, incredible builds,

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.540
but they often can't make money
from them.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.060
They don't have a good way to do it.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.300
I suggest using NFTs.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.950
You join the server
and build whatever you like,

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.720
then link your build to an NFT.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.400
You can list it for sale
or transfer it to someone else.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.160
Here's how it works.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.980
We open Minecraft
and connect to the server.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.980
Let's say we built this castle.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.600
Now we want to turn it into an NFT.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.050
We type /mint and give it a name.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:47.980
Then we paste the wallet address
of whoever will own the NFT.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:53.510
A few seconds later, our castle
is on Getgems as an NFT.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:57.660
We can list it for sale
or send it to someone.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.860
Now I'll show you how to load an NFT.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.220
We copy the NFT's address.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:09.780
Then we go back to Minecraft
and type /load.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:13.110
We paste the address,
and the world loads.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:17.980
We can fly past it,
but we can't interact with it.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:22.200
To interact with the build,
you need to own the NFT.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.780
We type /auth and follow the link.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.940
We can connect any wallet,
like Tonkeeper Desktop.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:35.980
If we own the NFT,
we can edit the build.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.040
Otherwise, we just fly past again.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:42.020
Who's the marketplace for?

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:47.820
Creative kids, artists,
and gaming content creators.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.130
Buyers include collectors
and server owners

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:56.350
who want to decorate their servers
or support the builders.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.930
What sets us apart?

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:02.050
We use blockchain and charge lower fees.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:05.580
You don't have to be over 18
or go through formal registration.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:09.500
Just connect a wallet
and you can start building right away.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.130
MNBT is a token
designed for viral growth.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:18.840
Every block you place earns tokens.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:24.560
The tokens go to the build's balance,
separate from the player's wallet.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:30.240
When you sell the build,
the rights to future airdrops go with it.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:35.980
That gives players a reason to build
and helps grow the market for builds.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:40.580
We have the youngest audience on TON.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:45.800
Today they play Minecraft.
Tomorrow they'll master the blockchain.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.100
That's it.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:52.100
Follow the link to find us on Instagram.
We're launching soon.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.040
Feel free to ask me questions.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.970
I'm easy to spot in the yellow shirt.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.170
[Host] Thanks so much. That was great!

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:03.980
By the way, Minecraft is officially
part of the school curriculum.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:06.980
In some schools in Russia, yes.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:10.980
Seriously, kids told me about it
a few years ago.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.450
Some Russian schools officially
added Minecraft to their curriculum.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.240
Well done!
